nts are detailed in the first book of Moses (Gen. 1:27-ch. 5).","verses":26,"father":"God","mother":"","v":[1,2,3,4,5]},{"id":"seth_2504","name":"Seth","also":"Sheth","summary":"Appointed; a substitute, the third son of Adam and Eve (Gen. 4:25; 5:3).","verses":10,"father":"Adam","mother":"Eve","v":[3,4,6,7,8]},{"id":"enos_1193","name":"Enos","also":"Enosh","summary":"Man the son of Seth, and grandson of Adam (Gen. 5:6-11; Luke 3:38). He lived nine hundred and five years.","verses":8,"father":"Seth","mother":"","v":[6,7,9,10,11]},{"id":"cainan_534","name":"Cainan","also":"Kenan","summary":"The fourth antediluvian patriarch, the eldest son of Enos. He was 70 years old at the birth of his eldest son Mahalaleel, after which he lived 840 years (Gen. 5:9-14), and was 910 years old when he died.","verses":7,"father":"Enos","mother":"","v":[9,10,12,13,14]},{"id":"mahalaleel_1885","name":"Mahalaleel","also":"Maleleel","summary":"The son of Cainan, of the line of Seth (Gen. 5:12-17); called Maleleel (Luke 3:37).","verses":7,"father":"Cainan","mother":"","v":[12,13,15,16,17]},{"id":"jared_730","name":"Jared","also":"Jered","summary":"The fourth antediluvian patriarch in descent from Seth (Gen. 5:15-20; Luke 3:37), the father of Enoch; called Jered in 1 Chr. 1:2.","verses":7,"father":"Mahalaleel","mother":"","v":[15,16,18,19,20]},{"id":"enoch_1192","name":"Enoch","also":"Henoch","summary":"The son of Jared, and father of Methuselah (Gen. 5:21; Luke 3:37). His father was one hundred and sixty-two years old when he was born. After the birth of Methuselah, Enoch “walked with God three hundred years” (Gen. 5:22-24), when he was translated without tasting death.","verses":10,"father":"Jared","mother":"","v":[18,19,21,22,23,24]},{"id":"methuselah_2042","name":"Methuselah","also":"Mathusala","summary":"Man of the dart, the son of Enoch, and grandfather of Noah.","verses":7,"father":"Enoch","mother":"","v":[21,22,25,26,27]},{"id":"lamech_1809","name":"Lamech","also":"","summary":"The seventh in descent from Seth, being the only son of Methuselah.","verses":7,"father":"Methuselah","mother":"","v":[25,26,28,30,31]},{"id":"noah_2210","name":"Noah","also":"Noe","summary":"Rest, (Heb. Noah) the grandson of Methuselah (Gen. 5:25-29), who was for two hundred and fifty years contemporary with Adam, and the son of Lamech, who was about fifty years old at the time of Adam’s death.","verses":47,"father":"Lamech","mother":"","v":[29,30,32]},{"id":"shem_2613","name":"Shem","also":"Sem","summary":"A name; renown, the first mentioned of the sons of Noah (Gen. 5:32; 6:10). He was probably the eldest of Noah’s sons. The words “brother of Japheth the elder” in Gen. 10:21 are more correctly rendered “the elder brother of Japheth,” as in the Revised Version.","verses":17,"father":"Noah","mother":"","v":[32]},{"id":"ham_1359","name":"Ham","also":"","summary":"Warm, hot, and hence the south; also an Egyptian word meaning “black”, the youngest son of Noah (Gen. 5:32; comp. 9:22, 24).","verses":14,"father":"Noah","mother":"","v":[32]},{"id":"japheth_726","name":"Japheth","also":"","summary":"Wide spreading: “God shall enlarge Japheth” (Heb. Yaphat Elohim le-Yephet, Gen. 9:27. Some, however, derive the name from yaphah, “to be beautiful;” hence white), one of the sons of Noah, mentioned last in order (Gen. 5:32; 6:10; 7:13), perhaps first by birth (10:21; comp. 9:24).","verses":11,"father":"Noah","mother":"","v":[32]}],"places":[],"events":[{"id":"birth_of_seth_7","title":"Birth of Seth","year":-3874,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 4:25 – Luke 3:38. People: Seth, Adam, Eve. Place: Eden.","v":[3]},{"id":"lifetime_of_adam_4","title":"Lifetime of Adam","year":-4004,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:3–5. People: Adam. Place: Eden. Lasted about 930 years.","v":[3,4,5]},{"id":"death_of_adam_23","title":"Death of Adam","year":-3074,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:5. People: Adam. Place: Eden.","v":[5]},{"id":"birth_of_enos_9","title":"Birth of Enos","year":-3769,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 4:26 – 1 Chronicles 1:1. People: Enos, Seth.","v":[6]},{"id":"lifetime_of_seth_8","title":"Lifetime of Seth","year":-3874,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:6–8. People: Seth. Lasted about 912 years.","v":[6,7,8]},{"id":"death_of_seth_25","title":"Death of Seth","year":-2962,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:8. People: Seth.","v":[8]},{"id":"birth_of_cainan_11","title":"Birth of Cainan","year":-3679,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:9 – Luke 3:37. People: Cainan, Enos.","v":[9]},{"id":"lifetime_of_enos_10","title":"Lifetime of Enos","year":-3769,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:9–11. People: Enos. Lasted about 905 years.","v":[9,10,11]},{"id":"death_of_enos_28","title":"Death of Enos","year":-2864,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:11. People: Enos.","v":[11]},{"id":"birth_of_mahlaleel_13","title":"Birth of Mahlaleel","year":-3609,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:12. People: Mahalaleel, Cainan.","v":[12]},{"id":"lifetime_of_cainan_12","title":"Lifetime of Cainan","year":-3679,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:12–14. People: Cainan. Lasted about 910 years.","v":[12,13,14]},{"id":"death_of_cainan_29","title":"Death of Cainan","year":-2769,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:14. People: Cainan.","v":[14]},{"id":"birth_of_jared_15","title":"Birth of Jared","year":-3544,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:15. People: Jared, Mahalaleel.","v":[15]},{"id":"lifetime_of_mahlaleel_14","title":"Lifetime of Mahlaleel","year":-3609,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:15–17. People: Mahalaleel. Lasted about 895 years.","v":[15,16,17]},{"id":"death_of_mahlaleel_30","title":"Death of Mahlaleel","year":-2714,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:17. People: Mahalaleel.","v":[17]},{"id":"birth_of_enoch_17","title":"Birth of Enoch","year":-3382,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:18. People: Enoch, Jared.","v":[18]},{"id":"lifetime_of_jared_16","title":"Lifetime of Jared","year":-3544,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 5:18–20. People: Jared. Lasted about 962 years.","v":[18,19,20]},{"id":"death_of_jared_31","title":"Death of Jared","year":-2582,"s